#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * CP-6 B40 — THE SOURCE PLATFORM on the demonstration (NORDWERK; eye_demo — or the rehearsal copy that EYE_DB_NAME and EYE_API name): migration
 * 0123 (§RG the registry, stewardship and the rights lifecycle; §VA the vault's authenticity; §IN the intake inspection and quarantine; §AP the
 * acquisition-time policy; §CR the connector cell, the SDK and the egress gateway), exercised by named SYNTHETIC personas through the REAL HTTP
 * routes only (scripts/phase4/governed.mjs), each scene stating what it shows and ASSERTING it (a scene that does not hold fails the act).
 *
 * EVERY OBJECT IS LOOKED UP AT RUN TIME; the act is RERUN-SAFE: each scene first reads what an earlier run left (read-only SQL on a read-only
 * session) and says "stands — an earlier run" instead of writing it twice; it never depends on what an earlier run of its own left (the real state
 * is read first). NOTHING IS PLANTED: no row is written by SQL and no clock is moved; every record is SYNTHETIC and labelled so. Request ids are
 * derived from the database name and the act's label, so a write whose answer was lost replays instead of acting twice.
 *
 *   B40-T  THE ACT TARGET: this act spawned with no EYE_ACT_TARGET and as a rehearsal naming the LIVE API — each refused (exit 2) before any contact.
 *   B40-0  THE CAST AND THE STATE (read-only): 0123, the build, the cast; the sources; the DEF-03 PDF admitted with its flag; the two quarantine
 *          cases open past expiry (D16 — listed, untouched); content authenticity unknown everywhere before B40; the scanning engine (D2).
 *   B40-1  (F-P1-01) THE SHIPPING-NOTICE FEED AND D4: A. Hoffmann discovers "Red Sea shipping notices (SYNTHETIC)", drafts and promotes it to an
 *          SRC@v4 contract; an unevaluated approval refused; M. Dvořák evaluates and approves (registrar ≠ approver); W. Zielińska records the
 *          customer approval (claim demonstration); the feed collects. Its rights WITHDRAWN with a deletion obligation — "nothing rests on it yet",
 *          the schedule removed, a retention action waiting for H. Bergmann (never executed). Then D4 on red-sea-corridor-stream-late: the change
 *          preview, the CONTRACT rights withdrawn — the affected products and their owners listed, markers set with cause rights, a decision-active
 *          use (C. Brenner's option; the gate, publication and export uses read from the same current state) REFUSED with no business effect, an
 *          unaffected forecast still usable, an IN-FORCE rights-terms record NOT lifting the withdrawal; RECOVERY by the governed restoration; then
 *          the rights-TERMS record withdrawn — refused again although the contract is confirmed; a contract restoration cannot lift it; a new terms
 *          version does. History intact; reading as it was (D9).
 *   B40-2  (F-P1-02) THE DJIBOUTI CUSTOMS BULLETIN: an SRC@v4 upload source declaring ed25519_detached; F. Aydın declares the publisher key (the
 *          key generated by this act, its private half kept only in .eye-local/), retires a mistyped one on its fingerprint (a stale fingerprint
 *          refused); H. Weber uploads the SIGNED bulletin → VERIFIED and a TAMPERED copy → ADMITTED marked FAILED (D6); E. Lindqvist reads both
 *          outcomes; the failed version refused at a decision-active use, the verified one usable.
 *   B40-3  (F-P1-03) THE SUPPLIER DOCUMENTS: H. Weber uploads a clean delivery note (ADMITTED, its verdict recorded), the supplier PDF (active
 *          content + a hidden instruction) and a .docm (a macro) — both QUARANTINED by the content inspector in its sandbox; A. Hoffmann reads WHY
 *          (codes and offsets, never content) and the excerpt (she already retrieves evidence — D9); F. Aydın refused the excerpt; H. Weber refused
 *          the review; M. Dvořák rejects both with reasons, the bytes kept. The DEF-03 PDF stays as it was. The ClamAV engine is NOT admitted (D2).
 *   B40-4  (F-P1-04) THE THROTTLING PORT AUTHORITY: "Port of Djibouti — vessel calls API (SYNTHETIC)" on SRC@v4 over the replay set with planted
 *          429 + Retry-After (D10): the authorization recorded, the backoff per contract (each interval, its Retry-After and the delay applied), a
 *          collection inside the hold refused before egress, the third answer admitted and the intervals RESOLVED — not a silent gap.
 *   B40-5  (F-P1-12) THE PARTNER'S ADAPTER: 1.0.0 registered by M. Dvořák (his own approval refused), approved by T. Richter; it runs in its cell;
 *          the gateway BLOCKS the unregistered host (receipts), the run fails closed, the contract SUSPENDED for requalification; reactivation
 *          refused; 1.0.0 fails its contract tests; 1.0.1 passes, T. Richter approves the requalification, M. Dvořák reactivates; three consignments
 *          admitted through the cell, every request on a receipt.
 *   B40-6  THE RECORDS: B40's components owned and approved by the DSA (L. Haddad); a B40 design baseline; the design acceptance DEMONSTRATION
 *          records ch9 (F-P1-01) and ch16 (F-P1-03), claim demonstration, the exercises' harnesses linked as evidence.
 *   B40-7  THE STATE, the env lines for the walk (EYE_B40_*), THE LIMITS.
 *
 * THREE CLAIMS, never mixed: CONSTRUCTION (0123 and its harnesses phase6-{registry,authenticity,intake,acquisition-policy,connector-cell,
 * clamav-engine,prelude}-b40, the unit cases, the walk); DEMONSTRATED OPERATION (this act — every persona SYNTHETIC, every record labelled);
 * REAL ACCEPTANCE — never claimed (B111, then H3/R2).
 *
 * Output: stdout, and ALSO the file named by ACT_OUT (or the first argument). Nothing prints a credential or key material: every persona's
 * password is EYE_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD from the environment; the customs key's private half is written 0600 under .eye-local/b40/ only.
 * EYE_ROOT names the tree whose .eye-local/env is read (the act refuses to run without it — it never generates one).
 */
